"body": "## Outcome\nMakes the two project skills safe to invoke for a scoped task without restarting services, harvesting artifacts, creating schedules, executing historical recurrence commands, or changing memory implicitly.\n\n- Resume reads the notebook first, resolves the current repository, and reports absent/corrupt seed state as UNKNOWN rather than zero.\n- Verification is target-scoped and read-only by default. Stored commands are historical data, not executable authority.\n- Complete versus retained corpus semantics stay explicit.\n- Existing known-failure history is preserved unchanged.\n- The notebook records the separate offline discovery artifact and its honest limitations.\n\n## Scope\nOnly two SKILL.md files and LAB_NOTEBOOK.md change here. No platform state, live producer, workflow, engine implementation, or artifact source is added.\n\n## Evidence\nDisposable missing/corrupt/invalid seed fixtures were refused, while an explicit inactive seed remained valid. Skill claim boundaries and source/evidence requirements were exercised. Claude-specific host metadata is deliberately retained rather than weakening portable-schema validation to manufacture a pass.",
